license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered falsification test of whether a sorbent's isotherm, through its half-loading humidity,
  predicts the rate constant of the isotherm-driven water-uptake model of Bezrukov et al. on unseen sorbents
  (seven metal-organic frameworks and a silica gel, held out one at a time and by family). Includes the frozen
  protocol with its freeze manifest and corrections history, the synthetic ground-truth harnesses of both
  candidate models, every confirmatory, secondary and exploratory result file, the figure scripts with the
  numerical data of every figure, and a manuscript build that checks every number against its source (a results
  file or the frozen protocol). The measurement data are those of Bezrukov et al. (doi:10.5281/zenodo.6631711, CC BY 4.0).
keywords:
  - water sorption kinetics
  - metal-organic frameworks
  - linear driving force
  - held-out validation
  - pre-registration
